  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in, and `npm test` passes (176 tests, 0 failed).\n\n- **Store (`src/store.js`)**:\n  - Added `reserve`, `getAvailable`, `confirm` and `release`.\n  - `removeItem` now fails with `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` if the quantity is more than what is available.\n  - Expiry is checked on every read against the store's `clock`, so nothing runs in the background.\n  - Ids look like `res-1`, `res-2`, and so on.\n- **API (`src/api.js`)**: `GET /stock/:sku` now also returns `available`. I added `POST /reservations`, `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` and `DELETE /reservations/:id` with the status codes you listed.\n- **Tests**: I added store and API tests for the new behavior.\n\nA few behaviors you didn't specify:\n- **`confirm` return value:** `store.confirm` returns the sku, which the API needs for its response.\n- **Expired reservations:** they stay in memory so that confirming one gives `RESERVATION_EXPIRED` rather than `RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND`. This means the reservations map grows over time.\n- **`ttlMs` is not validated:** a missing or non-numeric value gives a reservation that never counts as active.",
